# 125 - §6 (.37), the other half of 123: with no outer x ANYWHERE, the
# initialiser of `let x = x + 1;` has nothing to read, so it is a runtime Name
# error at the Var's line - raised while evaluating the initialiser, before any
# binding for x exists. Output is empty: the error is on line 1, so Display for
# Output renders only the error line.
#
# Name wording is taken from bead .39's table; error.rs is still a stub on
# master, so this is the only source for it (see bd_30-agents-2jk.55).
--- source
let x = x + 1;
print x;
--- expect
error: Name at line 1: undefined variable 'x'
